workedExamples.solution_text:
The hypotenuse is opposite the right angle. Relative to $\theta$, the opposite side is $12$ and the adjacent side is $16$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0)--(4,0)--(4,3)--cycle;
\draw[black] (3.7,0)--(3.7,0.3)--(4,0.3);
\draw[black] (0.65,0) arc[start angle=0,end angle=36.87,radius=0.65];
\path (0.9,0.3) node {$\theta$};
\path (2,0) node[below] {$16\ (A)$};
\path (4,1.5) node[right] {$12\ (O)$};
\path (2,1.5) node[above left] {$20\ (H)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}\sin\theta&=\frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{hypotenuse}}=\frac{12}{20}=\frac35\\\cos\theta&=\frac{\text{adjacent}}{\text{hypotenuse}}=\frac{16}{20}=\frac45\\\tan\theta&=\frac{\text{opposite}}{\text{adjacent}}=\frac{12}{16}=\frac34\end{aligned}$

