workedExamples.solution_text:
Name the sides from $\theta$, regardless of the triangle's orientation.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,every node/.style={font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont,text=black}]
\draw[black] (0,0)--(0,4)--(-3,0)--cycle;
\draw[black] (0,0.3)--(-0.3,0.3)--(-0.3,0);
\draw[black] (0,3.35) arc[start angle=270,end angle=233.13,radius=0.65];
\path (-0.3,3.05) node {$\theta$};
\path (0,2) node[right] {$v\ (A)$};
\path (-1.5,0) node[below] {$r\ (O)$};
\path (-1.5,2) node[above left] {$s\ (H)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{aligned}\sin\theta&=\frac{O}{H}=\frac{r}{s}\\\cos\theta&=\frac{A}{H}=\frac{v}{s}\\\tan\theta&=\frac{O}{A}=\frac{r}{v}\end{aligned}$

